eable files) and reads with errors='replace'","tests/unit/test_review_discovery_architecture.py:148-152 likewise swallows SyntaxError per file","A helper that eagerly parses every root file and raises on the first SyntaxError would change behaviour for the tolerant scanners"],"finding":"The plan's single parsed_python_files(root) helper does not specify how it reconciles per-scanner ast.parse parameter and error-handling divergence (filename=str(path), read encoding errors='replace', and try/except SyntaxError: continue), so its 'identical ASTs / behaviour-preserving' guarantee is not established for all in-scope scanners.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb4ee56f8413884a4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — 'identical file set, identical ASTs' and ParsedModule (path / relative / source / tree)","norm_id":"nbfc24427be0f3fc7","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A tree file that is intentionally unparseable (or partially planted) currently skipped by a tolerant scanner would make the shared helper raise, failing an unrelated migrated test","A migrated scanner that relied on filename=str(path) in a SyntaxError assertion produces a different message"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_